      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Storyboard Grid\n\nA **storyboard in one image**: describe a scene in beats, and Seed writes a grid prompt that Seedream paints as a pencil-sketch board with numbered panels.\n\n1. Rewrite **Scene beats (change me)**. Give each beat one clear action, say how many panels you want, and describe each recurring character and place once.\n2. Run. Read the prompt Seed wrote, then check **Save Image**.\n\nA sketch board is for deciding **staging and shot order**, not for polish. To keep faces and rooms consistent, connect your Character Sheet and Location Sheet images to `image_1`, `image_2` in the Seedream node and mention them in the beats (\"image 1 is the captain\").\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Storyboard Grid\n\nA **storyboard in one image**: describe a scene in beats, and Seed writes a grid prompt that Seedream paints as a pencil-sketch board with numbered panels.\n\n1. Rewrite **Scene beats (change me)**. Give each beat one clear action, say how many panels you want, and describe each recurring character and place once.\n2. Run. Read the prompt Seed wrote, then check **Save Image**.\n\nA sketch board is for deciding **staging and shot order**, not for polish. To keep faces and rooms consistent, connect your Character Sheet and Location Sheet images to `image_1`, `image_2` in the Seedream node and mention them in the beats (\"image 1 is the captain\").\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
